{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And you shall make your burnt-offerings.</b> If they are burnt-offerings, put the flesh and the blood on the altar; and if they are peace-offerings, \"the blood of your sacrifices shall be poured\" on the altar first and afterward \"the flesh you shall eat.\" And our Sages further expounded: \"Only your holy things\" comes to teach about offerings outside the Land, and to teach about substitutions and about the offspring of consecrated animals — that they are offered. (Sifrei; Bekhorot 14)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:50.966182107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}